===Regulations for EWC Club Championship===
* '''''Each club is restricted to only <span class="gold-text">one</span> duo during the Reload Series Finals at EWC
* '''''All players/duos must be signed and announced before <span class="gold-text">{{countdown|date=April 30th, 2026 - 23:59 {{Abbr/AST}}|rawdatetime=true}}</span> to be eligible for Club Points
** In case of a club qualifes multiple duos, only the duo who '''secured spots at the earliest time''' can represent the club
** Any other duo in this situation can still compete, but are '''not allowed to represent the club''' (i.e. wearing jerseys)

* '''''Rights to EWC Spots is tied to the <span class="gold-text">2 specific players who qualified together</span>
** If both cannot compete together as a pair, a '''replacement duo''' will be selected by EWC
** Roster lock is applied instantly after qualified, '''substitutes are not allowed'''
** If one half of the qualified duo drops out, they can re-attempt to qualify again with a new partner
** If a club releases an already qualified duo, they can re-attempt to qualify again with a new duo, however the new duo '''will not be eligible for Club Points'''
* '''''The aforementioned regulations does not apply to other modes and series outside EWC, such as FNCS

